<title>GERMANY: D.Telekom urges courage in EMU debate.</title>
<headline>D.Telekom urges courage in EMU debate.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The chairman of German telecommunications group Deutsche Telekom AG on Tuesday argued on behalf of Europe's single currency, planned to be introduced in 1999.</p>
<p>Germany, facing huge budget deficits and high unemployment that endanger its ability to qualify for European economic and monetary union, is embroiled in a discussion about whether the euro's introduction should be delayed.</p>
<p>Telekom chief Ron Sommer said at the company's annual news conference: &quot;As a globally-oriented company and good Europeans we ought to approach this issue with courage and not talk it to death.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097 145</p>
